# Luxora Brand Identity

## Brand Feel

Luxora Draws must always feel: **luxury, minimal, modern, confident, high-end**.

Never: chaotic, tacky, gimmicky, busy, or generic competition-site.

The design must feel established from day one — and must be capable of holding high-value prizes (watches, cars, luxury goods) as the brand scales.

## Fonts

Load all three from Google Fonts — no substitutions:

```html
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;0,900;1,400;1,500&family=Dancing+Script:wght@600&family=Jost:wght@300;400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

| Role | Font | Weights |
|------|------|---------|
| Headings, display, numbers | `Playfair Display` serif | 400, 500, 700, 900 + italic |
| Brand wordmark "draws" only | `Dancing Script` cursive | 600 |
| Body, UI, buttons, labels | `Jost` sans-serif | 300, 400, 500 |

Body base: `font-family: 'Jost', sans-serif; font-weight: 300; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;`

## Hard Rules

- **Sharp corners everywhere** — `border-radius: 0` on all buttons and cards; no rounded or pill shapes
- **No neon or bright colours** — stay within the defined palette only
- **No flashing or animated banners** — urgency is expressed through refined countdown timers only
- **No cheap badge graphics** — category labels use minimal text pills in brand colours
- **No cluttered layouts** — generous spacing and breathing room at all times
- **No loud sale banners** — offers and incentives must be presented elegantly
- **Uppercase labels use wide letter-spacing** (`0.16em`–`0.32em`), never tight
